{-
   Memory, as the machine has it.

   What is left in the portable file is the one operation both targets have under one name. The
   block copy and move, the ladder they are built out of and the system-call intrinsic are
   `Memory.native.yana`; the host's own block copy is `Memory.js.yana`. Analysis-Modules.md §2.5 is
   why those are files rather than attributes: eight of the nine declarations here carried the same
   `@platform(native)`, which is a property of the *file* being read out loud nine times.
-}

-- The fill. One name on both targets: natively it is the machine's store-a-byte-n-times, and on JS
-- it is what the relocation glue opens a fresh host array with.
pub fn setMemory(to: %U8, value: U8, count: Size) -> {}
